IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART II National Employment Service: regs 58 and 59.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation
-- current to 2026-09-30; unofficial, and nothing here claims to be verified against the official text.
--
-- THE RELATION. Regs 58 and 59 put a duty on the Commission (it maintains the national employment service under
-- ss 60(1) and (2) of the Act) and give a claim to the persons served: workers, employers, workers' organizations
-- and organizations providing employment assistance. The Commission appears here only as the holder of the duty;
-- every rule is named for what it decides between the service and the user, not from one side.
-- "Where appropriate" (58(c)(ii)) and "when necessary" (58(c)(iv)) hand a judgment to the service; each is a
-- BOOLEAN input named for that judgment and is never guessed (fork F1).
-- No section GIVEN: every rule has its own GIVEN.

§ `Regulation 58 -- what the national employment service does`

-- The lead-in of reg 58 gives the purpose (facilitating the fullest possible integration into the Canadian work
-- force of persons who need assistance in competing in the labour market) and the manner (in cooperation with
-- interested public authorities, employers, unions and organizations representing industries and industrial
-- sectors). A purpose is not a condition: reg 59 makes the service available to ALL workers (fork F2).

§§ `Regulation 58(a) -- information collected and analysed`

-- src:994 | 58 The national employment service maintained by the Commission under subsections 60(1) and (2) of the Act shall, for the purpose of facilitating the fullest possible integration into the Canadian work force of persons who need assistance in competing in the labour market, in cooperation with interested public authorities, employers, unions and organizations representing industries and industrial sectors,
-- src:995 | (a) collect and analyse the available information on the situation of the labour market, including information on labour market supply and demand, the economic and employment situations of individuals, families and communities, career and learning trends, and social and community conditions, and its probable evolution, both in Canada as a whole and in different industries, occupations and areas;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58 lead-in and (a) (src:994-995)
DECLARE `er4 Information the national employment service collects and analyses` IS ONE OF
    `er4 the situation of the labour market`
    `er4 labour market supply and demand`
    `er4 the economic and employment situations of individuals, families and communities`
    `er4 career and learning trends`
    `er4 social and community conditions`
    `er4 the probable evolution of the labour market`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(a) (src:995)
DECLARE `er4 Level at which the national employment service collects information` IS ONE OF
    `er4 Canada as a whole`
    `er4 different industries`
    `er4 different occupations`
    `er4 different areas`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(a) (src:995)
GIVETH A LIST OF `er4 Information the national employment service collects and analyses`
`reg 58(a) the information the national employment service is to collect and analyse` MEANS
    LIST `er4 the situation of the labour market`
       , `er4 labour market supply and demand`
       , `er4 the economic and employment situations of individuals, families and communities`
       , `er4 career and learning trends`
       , `er4 social and community conditions`
       , `er4 the probable evolution of the labour market`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(a) (src:995)
GIVETH A LIST OF `er4 Level at which the national employment service collects information`
`reg 58(a) the levels at which the national employment service is to collect and analyse it` MEANS
    LIST `er4 Canada as a whole`
       , `er4 different industries`
       , `er4 different occupations`
       , `er4 different areas`

§§ `Regulation 58(b) -- the information is made available`

-- src:996 | (b) make that information available systematically and promptly to interested public authorities, the employers' and workers' organizations concerned and the general public;
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(b) (src:996)
DECLARE `er4 Recipient of labour market information` IS ONE OF
    `er4 an interested public authority`
    `er4 an employers' organization concerned`
    `er4 a workers' organization concerned`
    `er4 a member of the general public`
    `er4 someone else`

-- Every recipient the text names is entitled; anyone else is not mentioned, so the answer for them is NOTHING
-- (not covered), never FALSE: the text does not say that someone else may not be given the information.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(b) (src:996)
GIVEN recipient IS A `er4 Recipient of labour market information`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` recipient MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `er4 someone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Regulation 58(c) -- help to workers`

-- Paragraph (c) helps "workers" in each of its five limbs; each limb below therefore takes whether the person is a worker.
-- "Worker" is not defined in the Act or the Regulations, so it is a BOOLEAN input.
-- src:997 | (c) help workers find suitable employment by
-- src:998 | (i) making available to them information on employment opportunities locally, regionally and nationally, including information on specific job openings as well as general information on careers and occupations that are in demand in the labour market and the educational and skill requirements for those careers or occupations,
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(i) (src:997-998)
GIVEN `the person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(c)(i) the national employment service is to make available information on employment opportunities and on careers and occupations in demand to` MEANS
    `the person is a worker`

-- src:999 | (ii) where appropriate, referring them to other sources of labour market information such as social service agencies and community employment services organizations,
-- "Where appropriate": whose judgment is not said; it is the service's, as it decides whether to refer (fork F1).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(ii) (src:999)
GIVEN `the person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate to refer the worker to other sources of labour market information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(c)(ii) the national employment service is to refer a worker to other sources of labour market information` MEANS
        `the person is a worker`
    AND `it is appropriate to refer the worker to other sources of labour market information`

-- src:1000 | (iii) obtaining from workers seeking employment such information as is necessary to effect proper referrals to employment opportunities within Canada and abroad,
-- Only workers "seeking employment" are named in (iii).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(iii) (src:1000)
GIVEN `the person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker is seeking employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(c)(iii) the national employment service is to obtain from a worker the information necessary to effect proper referrals` MEANS
        `the person is a worker`
    AND `the worker is seeking employment`

-- src:1001 | (iv) in accordance with local community-based service and client targeting strategies, interviewing and counselling workers, when necessary, to assess their employment needs and assist them to develop action plans in order to address those needs, and
-- Two conditions on the service's side: "in accordance with local community-based service and client targeting
-- strategies" and "when necessary" (fork F1: both are judgments the text leaves to the service).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(iv) (src:1001)
GIVEN `the person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `local community-based service and client targeting strategies call for interviewing and counselling the worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary to interview and counsel the worker to assess their employment needs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(c)(iv) the national employment service is to interview and counsel a worker and help them develop action plans` MEANS
        `the person is a worker`
    AND `local community-based service and client targeting strategies call for interviewing and counselling the worker`
    AND `it is necessary to interview and counsel the worker to assess their employment needs`

-- src:1002 | (v) providing them with information on the availability of special assistance where they are experiencing particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment; and
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(c)(v) (src:1002)
GIVEN `the person is a worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the worker is experiencing particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 58(c)(v) the national employment service is to provide a worker with information on the availability of special assistance` MEANS
        `the person is a worker`
    AND `the worker is experiencing particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment`

§§ `Regulation 58(d) -- help to employers`

-- src:1003 | (d) help employers find suitable workers by
-- src:1004 | (i) obtaining from them information on job vacancies and such information as is necessary to effect proper referrals of workers to the employers,
-- src:1005 | (ii) advising them on various ways to meet their employment needs, and
-- src:1006 | (iii) making available to them information on workers searching for employment.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(d) (src:1003-1006)
DECLARE `er4 Help the national employment service gives an employer` IS ONE OF
    `er4 obtaining information on job vacancies and the information necessary to effect proper referrals of workers`
    `er4 advising on various ways to meet their employment needs`
    `er4 making available information on workers searching for employment`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 58(d) (src:1003-1006)
GIVETH A LIST OF `er4 Help the national employment service gives an employer`
`reg 58(d) the help the national employment service is to give an employer to find suitable workers` MEANS
    LIST `er4 obtaining information on job vacancies and the information necessary to effect proper referrals of workers`
       , `er4 advising on various ways to meet their employment needs`
       , `er4 making available information on workers searching for employment`

§ `Regulation 59 -- the service is free`

-- src:1007 | 59 The national employment service shall be made available at no cost to all workers whether insured or not or whether they are claiming unemployment benefits or not, and to all employers, workers' organizations and interested public and private organizations providing employment assistance services to workers.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 59 (src:1007)
DECLARE `er4 User of the national employment service` IS ONE OF
    `er4 a worker`
    `er4 an employer`
    `er4 a workers' organization`
    `er4 an interested public or private organization providing employment assistance services to workers`
    `er4 someone else`

-- Whether a worker is insured, and whether they are claiming unemployment benefits, makes no difference to
-- the answer, so neither is an input. A user the text does not name gets NOTHING (not covered).
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 59 (src:1007)
GIVEN user IS A `er4 User of the national employment service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` user MEANS
    CONSIDER user
    WHEN `er4 someone else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
